+# Generative Fallbacks & Runbook
+
+This runbook describes fallback behaviors and operator steps when a generation path is suppressed or a verifier/policy check fails.
+
+Fallback behavior (default)
+- If policy_enforce denies content, the middleware replaces response with FALLBACK_TEXT (configurable) and logs audit record.
+- If verifier is unreachable during pre-check, conservative behavior is to fallback and create incident.
+- If candidate model divergence in canary exceeds threshold, rollback to previous model and open incident.
+
+Operator steps when fallback observed
+1) Identify incident: check logs in evidence S3 under gen_shadow/ or audit logs with key agent_audit/policy_block.
+2) Inspect provenance: model_id, model_version, artifact_sig in response/provenance.
+3) Replay input against prod model and candidate model locally using tests/generative/canary_eval.py.
+4) If verifier misconfiguration suspected, run services/factuality/verifier_calibration_on_holdout.py on SME holdout and republish ConfigMap.
+5) If model regression observed, rollback via kubectl -n safety set image deployment/verifier verifier=<previous-image> and patch ModelPromotion as failed.
+6) Notify ML Lead, Security, and SRE per on-call roster and attach evidence link to S3 objects.
+
+Automation & alerts
+- Prometheus alerts: MultimodalEmbeddingDrift, ShadowDivergence, VerifierRegression.
+- On severe divergence, circuit-breaker automatically disables promotions and flags SRE.
+
